WEBVTT

00:00.670 --> 00:06.060
We're told this table shows
equivalent ratios to 24 to 40.

00:06.060 --> 00:07.820
Fill in the missing values.

00:07.820 --> 00:10.450
And they write the ratio
24 to 40 right over here.

00:10.450 --> 00:14.720
24-- when the numerator is
24, the denominator is 40.

00:14.720 --> 00:16.631
So in that way, you
could think of 24/40.

00:16.631 --> 00:18.630
But then they want us to
write equivalent ratios

00:18.630 --> 00:20.520
where we have to fill
in different blanks

00:20.520 --> 00:22.090
over here-- here
in the denominator

00:22.090 --> 00:23.370
and here in the numerator.

00:23.370 --> 00:25.994
And there's a bunch of ways that
we could actually tackle this.

00:25.994 --> 00:27.994
But maybe the easiest is
to start with the ratio

00:27.994 --> 00:29.535
that they gave us,
where they gave us

00:29.535 --> 00:31.410
both the numerator
and the denominator,

00:31.410 --> 00:32.710
and then move from there.

00:32.710 --> 00:35.640
So for example, if we look
at this one right over here,

00:35.640 --> 00:36.950
the numerator is 12.

00:36.950 --> 00:39.220
It is half of the 24.

00:39.220 --> 00:42.310
So the denominator is also going
to be half of the denominator

00:42.310 --> 00:42.810
here.

00:42.810 --> 00:44.460
It's going to be half of 40.

00:44.460 --> 00:48.000
So we could stick a
20 right over there.

00:48.000 --> 00:49.500
And then we could go up here.

00:49.500 --> 00:52.960
If you compare the 3 to
the 12, to go from 12 to 3,

00:52.960 --> 00:54.460
you have to divide by 4.

00:54.460 --> 00:56.474
So in the numerator,
you're dividing by 4.

00:56.474 --> 00:58.640
So in the denominator, you
also want to divide by 4.

00:58.640 --> 01:01.889
So 20 divided by 4 is 5.

01:01.889 --> 01:03.430
And then we have
one more to fill in,

01:03.430 --> 01:04.881
this numerator right over here.

01:04.881 --> 01:07.380
And we see from the denominator,
we doubled the denominator.

01:07.380 --> 01:09.880
We went from 40 to 80.

01:09.880 --> 01:11.810
So we would double
the numerator as well,

01:11.810 --> 01:14.240
and so you would get 48.

01:14.240 --> 01:17.370
And what we just did here is we
wrote four equivalent ratios.

01:17.370 --> 01:21.730
The ratio 3 to 5 or 3/5 is
the same thing as 12 to 20,

01:21.730 --> 01:26.830
is the same thing as 24 to 40,
is the same thing as 48 to 80.

01:26.830 --> 01:28.800
Let's make sure we
got the right answer.

01:28.800 --> 01:31.470
Let's do a couple more of these.

01:31.470 --> 01:37.280
The following table shows
equivalent fractions to 27/75.

01:37.280 --> 01:41.130
So then they wrote all of the
different equivalent fractions.

01:41.130 --> 01:45.180
This table shows ratios
equivalent to 18/55.

01:45.180 --> 01:45.930
Fair enough.

01:45.930 --> 01:50.280
All right, so these are
all equivalent to 27/75.

01:50.280 --> 01:54.910
These are all equivalent
to 18/55, so all of these.

01:54.910 --> 02:01.480
Which fraction is
greater, 27/75 or 18/55?

02:01.480 --> 02:03.100
So this is an interesting thing.

02:03.100 --> 02:05.190
What we want to do-- because
you look at these two things.

02:05.190 --> 02:06.390
And you're like,
well, I don't know.

02:06.390 --> 02:07.990
Their denominators
are different.

02:07.990 --> 02:09.740
How do I compare them?

02:09.740 --> 02:12.000
And the best way that I
can think of comparing them

02:12.000 --> 02:15.950
is look at a point where you're
getting an equivalent fraction.

02:15.950 --> 02:18.646
And either the numerators
are going to be the same,

02:18.646 --> 02:20.520
or the denominators are
going to be the same.

02:20.520 --> 02:22.800
So let's see if there's
any situation here.

02:22.800 --> 02:30.300
So you have this situation
where we see 27/75 is 54/150.

02:30.300 --> 02:34.140
And over here, we see
that 18/55 is 54--

02:34.140 --> 02:36.190
and this 54 jumped
out at me because it's

02:36.190 --> 02:39.100
the same numerator-- over 165.

02:39.100 --> 02:40.920
And that makes the
comparison much easier.

02:40.920 --> 02:42.520
What is smaller?

02:42.520 --> 02:45.716
54/150 or 54/165?

02:48.410 --> 02:50.150
Well, if you have
the same numerator,

02:50.150 --> 02:53.630
having a larger denominator
will make the number smaller.

02:53.630 --> 02:58.790
So 54/165 is smaller than
54/150, which tells us

02:58.790 --> 03:03.802
that 18/55 is
smaller than 27/75.

03:03.802 --> 03:05.010
So let's see, which of these?

03:05.010 --> 03:10.030
So this is saying that
27/75 is greater than 18/55,

03:10.030 --> 03:12.460
and that is absolutely right.

03:12.460 --> 03:16.220
And let's do one more of these.

03:16.220 --> 03:18.840
Lunara's friends
are running a race.

03:18.840 --> 03:22.910
Each of them runs at a constant
speed starting at time 0.

03:22.910 --> 03:25.950
Which of these tables might
show the distances one

03:25.950 --> 03:29.337
of Lunara's friends
traveled over time?

03:29.337 --> 03:30.420
So they're running a race.

03:30.420 --> 03:33.110
Each of them runs at a constant
speed starting at time 0.

03:33.110 --> 03:38.560
So table 1-- so
distance run in meters.

03:38.560 --> 03:41.550
So they're running
at a constant speed.

03:41.550 --> 03:45.340
So really, the ratio
between distance and time

03:45.340 --> 03:49.770
should be constant throughout
all of these possible tables.

03:49.770 --> 03:51.910
So here you have
a ratio of 3 to 2.

03:51.910 --> 03:55.290
If you triple the distance,
we're tripling the time.

03:55.290 --> 03:58.090
If you multiply
the distance by 5,

03:58.090 --> 04:00.400
we're multiplying the time by 5.

04:00.400 --> 04:02.850
So table 1 seems
completely reasonable.

04:02.850 --> 04:03.620
Let's keep going.

04:03.620 --> 04:08.280
Table 2-- 11 to 4
and then 12 to 5.

04:08.280 --> 04:09.720
Here, it's just
incrementing by 1,

04:09.720 --> 04:11.210
but the ratios are not the same.

04:11.210 --> 04:14.170
11 to 4 is not the
same thing as 12 to 5.

04:14.170 --> 04:18.589
So we're not going to be able
to-- this right over here

04:18.589 --> 04:23.100
is not a legitimate table.

04:23.100 --> 04:26.210
Table 3-- so 1 to 1.

04:26.210 --> 04:28.980
Then when you double the
distance, we double the time.

04:28.980 --> 04:33.180
When you triple the
distance from 1,

04:33.180 --> 04:34.490
you didn't triple the time.

04:34.490 --> 04:37.050
So table 3 doesn't seem
to make sense, either.

04:37.050 --> 04:40.480
Table 4-- so 14 to 10.

04:40.480 --> 04:42.530
So that's the same
thing as-- let's see,

04:42.530 --> 04:45.920
that's the same ratio as, if
we were to divide by 2, as

04:45.920 --> 04:48.280
7 to 5 ratio.

04:48.280 --> 04:52.170
If we divide both of these by
3, this is also a 7 to 5 ratio.

04:52.170 --> 04:55.140
And if you divide both of these
by 7, this is also a 7 to 5

04:55.140 --> 04:55.980
ratio.

04:55.980 --> 05:01.130
So table 4 seems like a
completely reasonable scenario.

05:01.130 --> 05:04.740
And we can check our
answer, and it is.
